<BaseLayout title="About BIRDS" description="Learn about BIRDS, an independent journal celebrating the fascinating world of birds.">
  <section class="about-hero container"><span class="eyebrow">OUR LITTLE CORNER OF THE NATURAL WORLD</span><h1>For the love of <em>birds.</em></h1><p class="about-lead">BIRDS is an independent journal built around one simple idea: the more we notice the natural world, the more connected we become to it.</p><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1444464666168-49d633b86797?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=85" alt="A bird resting among branches" /></section>
  <section class="container about-content"><div><span class="eyebrow">WHY WE’RE HERE</span><h2>Curiosity takes flight.</h2></div><div class="prose"><p>From the smallest garden visitor to the great travellers crossing continents, birds have a remarkable way of making us pause. Their colours, calls, migrations and adaptations tell stories about the places we share.</p><p>We publish accessible articles, thoughtful guides and nature notes for readers at every level. Whether you are learning to identify your first bird or deepening a lifelong interest, there is always something new to discover.</p><p>Our aim is simple: share useful knowledge, encourage respectful observation and celebrate the extraordinary lives of birds.</p><a class="button button-dark" href="/articles/">Read our stories <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>